cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research prototype, cite the software and its declared interpretation boundary."
title: "Recursive Resolution Closure Theory: Nonvalenced Research Prototype"
type: software
version: 0.37.0-dev1
date-released: 2026-08-21
authors:
  - family-names: "P."
    given-names: "Komorebi"
abstract: >-
  A bounded NumPy implementation of nested resolution projectors, specialist
  processors, recurrent global workspace, trained and frozen causal self-model,
  episodic memory, independently controlled recurrence and explicit feedback
  paths, prospective self-counterfactual control, learned observation forecasting,
  auditable one-sided intervention calibration, Bayesian causal-transfer
  correction with portable posterior receipts, formal closure cut certificates,
  piecewise-local state-transition diagnostics, spectrum-preserving predictor
  controls, agent-owned prospective causal-boundary discovery, online
  self-model revision and native workspace access, and multi-seed functional
  diagnostics. Version 0.31 adds cross-fitted, lower-mode-preserving
  conditional operational-rank inference and persistent two-window boundary
  admission. Its frozen official result has integrity PASS but scientific FAIL
  after one conditional rank-one null flips three coupled primary gates.
  Version 0.36 adds one persistent truth-free boundary/action runtime and a
  single-seed exploratory pilot. Initial discovered-boundary action succeeded;
  later structural recovery was terminal and had no post-change action tail.
  Version 0.36.0-dev2 hardens future evidence retention without opening another
  seed. Version 0.37 adds fixed post-change action tails, fail-closed public
  certificate quarantine, one-step transition-model rollout, and paired
  no-certificate, stale-certificate, and shuffled-identity controls under a
  pre-outcome campaign freeze. The software does not claim to create or detect
  phenomenal consciousness.
